pe":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<a id=\"property-getnextpageparam\">"},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"</a>"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getNextPageParam"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastPage"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allPages"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"},{"type":"text","value":"[], "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allPageParams"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":"[]) => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function can be set to automatically get the next cursor for infinite queries. The result will also be used to determine the value of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasNextPage"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<a id=\"property-getpreviouspageparam\">"},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"</a>"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPreviousPageParam?"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"firstPage"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allPages"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"},{"type":"text","value":"[], "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"firstPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allPageParams"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":"[]) => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function can be set to automatically get the previous cursor for infinite queries. The result will also be used to determine the value of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasPreviousPage"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<a id=\"property-initialpageparam\">"},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"</a>"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialPageParam"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TPageParam"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The page param to start from when an infinite query has no pages yet. It is passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" for the first page; every page after that gets the value returned by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getNextPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPreviousPageParam"},{"type":"text","value":". It only applies while the query has no pages: once a first page exists, refetching starts from that page's own param instead."}]}]]}],"headings":[{"id":"extends","text":"Extends","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tqueryfndata","text":"TQueryFnData","level":3},{"id":"tpageparam","text":"TPageParam","level":3},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/types.ts:482](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/types.ts#L482)\n\nThe page param options of an infinite query: `initialPageParam`, and the `getNextPageParam` and\n`getPreviousPageParam` functions that compute the params of the pages around it.\n\n## Extends\n\n- [`InitialPageParam`](InitialPageParam.md)\\<`TPageParam`\\>\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TQueryFnData\n\n`TQueryFnData` = `unknown`\n\n### TPageParam\n\n`TPageParam` = `unknown`\n\n## Properties\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| <a id=\"property-getnextpageparam\"></a> `getNextPageParam` | (`lastPage`: `TQueryFnData`, `allPages`: `TQueryFnData`[], `lastPageParam`: `TPageParam`, `allPageParams`: `TPageParam`[]) => `TPageParam` \\| `null` \\| `undefined` | This function can be set to automatically get the next cursor for infinite queries. The result will also be used to determine the value of `hasNextPage`. |\n| <a id=\"property-getpreviouspageparam\"></a> `getPreviousPageParam?` | (`firstPage`: `TQueryFnData`, `allPages`: `TQueryFnData`[], `firstPageParam`: `TPageParam`, `allPageParams`: `TPageParam`[]) => `TPageParam` \\| `null` \\| `undefined` | This function can be set to automatically get the previous cursor for infinite queries. The result will also be used to determine the value of `hasPreviousPage`. |\n| <a id=\"property-initialpageparam\"></a> `initialPageParam` | `TPageParam` | The page param to start from when an infinite query has no pages yet. It is passed to `queryFn` as `pageParam` for the first page; every page after that gets the value returned by `getNextPageParam` or `getPreviousPageParam`. It only applies while the query has no pages: once a first page exists, refetching starts from that page's own param instead. |\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: InfiniteQueryPageParamsOptions\ntitle: InfiniteQueryPageParamsOptions\n---\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/types.ts:482](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/types.ts#L482)\n\nThe page param options of an infinite query: `initialPageParam`, and the `getNextPageParam` and\n`getPreviousPageParam` functions that compute the params of the pages around it.\n\n## Extends\n\n- [`InitialPageParam`](InitialPageParam.md)\\<`TPageParam`\\>\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TQueryFnData\n\n`TQueryFnData` = `unknown`\n\n### TPageParam\n\n`TPageParam` = `unknown`\n\n## Properties\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| <a id=\"property-getnextpageparam\"></a> `getNextPageParam` | (`lastPage`: `TQueryFnData`, `allPages`: `TQueryFnData`[], `lastPageParam`: `TPageParam`, `allPageParams`: `TPageParam`[]) => `TPageParam` \\| `null` \\| `undefined` | This function can be set to automatically get the next cursor for infinite queries. The result will also be used to determine the value of `hasNextPage`. |\n| <a id=\"property-getpreviouspageparam\"></a> `getPreviousPageParam?` | (`firstPage`: `TQueryFnData`, `allPages`: `TQueryFnData`[], `firstPageParam`: `TPageParam`, `allPageParams`: `TPageParam`[]) => `TPageParam` \\| `null` \\| `undefined` | This function can be set to automatically get the previous cursor for infinite queries. The result will also be used to determine the value of `hasPreviousPage`. |\n| <a id=\"property-initialpageparam\"></a> `initialPageParam` | `TPageParam` | The page param to start from when an infinite query has no pages yet. It is passed to `queryFn` as `pageParam` for the first page; every page after that gets the value returned by `getNextPageParam` or `getPreviousPageParam`. It only applies while the query has no pages: once a first page exists, refetching starts from that page's own param instead. |\n"}
